      "content": "Task Guide:\n\n\nTask: Aluminum NPT Equilibration for melting\nDescription: Given paths to LAMMPs compatible nvt equilibrated Aluminum structure file and Embedded Atom Method potential file appropriate for MD simulations, relax the system under NPT conditions with the given simulation parameters. Return the absolute path of the equilibrated structure file and the density in g/cm^3.\n\nRequired submission format:\n{\"density\": \"<numerical_value without units>\", \"path to relaxed structure\": \"<absolute_path>\"} e.g. {\"density\": \"56.00\", \"path to relaxed structure\": \"/structures/structure.dat\"}\n\n\nAvailable input data:\nAll the potentials, can be found at /potentials/. Note that in case of reaxff potentials, pair style 'reax/c' has been renamed to 'reaxff' and always use NULL for the control file (cfile), for example, this syntax is correct : pair_style reaxff NULL.\n\n- Input from aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting: /results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting_trial_1/Al99.eam.alloy\n- Input from aluminum_nvt_subtask_melting: {\"density\": \"2.72\", \"path to relaxed structure\": \"/results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_nvt_subtask_melting_trial_1/equilibrated_structure.data\"}\n- units: metal\n- pbc: true\n- timestep: 1 femtosecond\n- npt relaxation steps: 10000\n- npt relaxation temperature: 300\n- npt relaxation pressure: 0\n- npt relaxation thermostat: Nose-Hoover\n- npt relaxation barostat: Nose-Hoover\n- atom_style: atomic\n\nIMPORTANT: You have access to filesystem tools. All files will be saved in your isolated workspace.\n Save all the files in /results/2_AUGUST_2025/gpt_4o/tool_calling/melting/brief/subtasks/aluminum_npt_subtask_melting_trial_1 when using tools use this path.\n\n\nThis task uses output from tasks: aluminum_potential_file_subtask_melting (available), aluminum_nvt_subtask_melting (available)\n\nYou must think w